import math

# 3-Phase Power Calculator

VL = float(input("Enter Line Voltage (V): "))
IL = float(input("Enter Line Current (A): "))
power_factor = float(input("Enter Power Factor: "))

power = math.sqrt(3) * VL * IL * power_factor

print("3-Phase Power =", power, "Watts")
print("3-Phase Power =", power / 1000, "kW")


Formula:

$$ P = \sqrt{3}\times V_L\times I_L\times \cos\phi $$

Where:

VL = Line Voltage (V)
IL = Line Current (A)
cosφ = Power Factor
P = 3-Phase Power (W)



vExample

If:

Voltage = 400 V
Current = 10 A
Power Factor = 0.8

Output:

3-Phase Power = 5542.56 W
Power = 5.54 kW
